  "answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 with a focus on leveraging AI to improve efficiency (potentially by 20%) and data visualization tools. Key milestones include the completion of the design phase, the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, and the expansion of the team with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. The project is currently moving into the development phase, with lead developer Omar Jensen providing guidance. Upcoming activities include user interface enhancements in October, a feedback collection period ending in November, and the implementation of updated security protocols (multi-factor authentication and encryption) starting next January. Additionally, a training budget of $15,000 has been approved for the coding team and project managers, with sessions starting next month."
